  "hindi": "जिसने, बृहस्पति ने, तीन आसनों वाले होकर, बल से और गर्जन से पृथ्वी के छोरों को अलग-अलग थामा; उसे प्राचीन ऋषियों ने चिन्तन करते हुए, विप्रों ने, आगे रखा, मनोहर जीभ वाले को।",
  "english": "Bṛhaspati, who, three-seated, with force and with a roar propped apart the ends of the earth — him the ancient sages, contemplating, the inspired ones, placed in front, the one with the pleasing tongue.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "yaḥ ... bṛhaspatiḥ triṣadhasthaḥ: the relative clause is joined with raveṇa as the manner. dīdhyānāḥ (√dīdhī) can also be \"shining\"; \"contemplating\" chosen. mandra = pleasing/gladdening; jihvā = tongue.",
  "confidence": "high"
